WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.830
- So MSCHF Product Studios
teamed up with rapper, Lil Nas X

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.950
to modify some Nike shoes
that were made with a splash

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.420
of real human blood.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.840
Nike says just don't do it.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.770
And following in the
footsteps of cultural icons

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.200
like 17th century poet, John
Milton and Madonna, the singer,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.440
not the other one,

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.790
Lil Nas X dropped a music video
where he evokes Satan's fall

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:24.240
into hell by descending into
hell himself via stripper pole.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.570
I don't think that is
actually in "Paradise Lost".

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.410
But along the way, Lil Nas X wears

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.740
modified Nike Air Max 97s.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.410
MSCHF Product Studio was
responsible for modding the shoes,

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.430
adding occult references like 666,

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.530
a pentagram, Bible verses in red ink.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:39.950
Oh, and of course, the midsole

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:43.210
of each shoe contains exactly
one drop of human blood.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.610
But when MSCHF offered 666
pairs of shoes for sale,

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.570
Nike responded quickly by suing MSCHF

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.620
for trademark infringement.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.816
So the question is what
the hell is going on?

00:00:52.816 --> 00:00:55.100
(triumphant music)

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.840
Sponsored by Skillshare

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.673
Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:00:57.673 --> 00:00:58.680
It's time to think like a lawyer

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.800
because the devil is in the details.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.640
And what is going on with this suit?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.930
What does it mean for
sneaker heads in general?

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.720
Is it illegal to modify a
consumer product and resell it?

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.850
Does this mean that you can't
sell modified Nikes anymore,

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.130
or any other kind of modified clothing?

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.020
Well, we're going to get
into all of that today

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.480
because this is a fascinating
case that just involves

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.380
just about everything.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.630
But first a point of clarification

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.230
because a lot of people
think that this case

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:26.050
involves copyright and
that's simply not the case.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.500
There are generally three
kinds of intellectual property

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.700
or IP that people think about.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.950
There's copyright patent and trademark.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.950
Copyright involves things
that are expressive.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.600
Things like art, books, TV shows, movies,

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.210
that gets copyright protection.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.170
Then there's patents.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.400
That tends to cover useful
items, things like inventions.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.280
And then finally, that leaves trademark,

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.410
which is meant to protect
the consumer public.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:51.090
It's meant to show
people where things came

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.650
from by creating brands so
that they know the source

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.520
of the things that they are buying.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.920
And in order to qualify
for trademark protection

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.960
under federal law,

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.290
a trademark has to meet
three basic requirements.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.160
One, the trademark has to
be distinctive of the source

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.220
of the goods or services
to which it is affixed.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.030
Number two, the trademark
must not be disqualified

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.450
from protection by various
statutory bars to protection.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:17.080
And number three, the trademark
has to be used in commerce.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.670
The purpose of trademark
is to identify the source

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.610
of goods to ensure that consumers

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.700
actually know where
their products come from.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.090
In other words, trademark
holders get protection

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.450
from people and companies who
would sell knockoff goods.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.580
It's all about protecting
the consumer public.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.260
And that's what this
whole lawsuit is about.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.197
Nike has invested billions
of dollars into its brand,

00:02:37.197 --> 00:02:39.310
and is trying to protect the strength

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.910
of the Swoosh and the Nike word mark

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.600
so that people aren't confused

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.380
and people don't think that
Nike created some shoes

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.900
that are endorsed by Satan.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.910
You can sort of understand

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.300
where they're coming from on that.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.210
And in Nike's lawsuit, it
immediately dissociates itself

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.410
from the Satan Shoes.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.000
Quote, "MSCHF is currently taking orders

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.940
for the shoes it refers
to as these Satan Shoes,

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.560
which are customized Nike Air Max 97 shoes

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.260
that MSCHF has materially
altered to prominently feature

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.650
a satanic theme.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.250
This was done without Nike's
approval or authorization.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.860
And Nike is in no way
connected to this project."

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.510
So Nike brings a bunch of claims.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.340
And the first of which is garden variety

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.730
trademark infringement in
violation of 15 U.S.C. 1114.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:19.010
And Nike claims that
MSCHF products violated

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.590
Nike's trademark by manufacturing
and selling Satan Shoes.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.850
So how do you prove
trademark infringement?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.497
Well, to prevail on a claim
of trademark infringement,

00:03:26.497 --> 00:03:29.550
the company has to show one,
it owns a valid trademark.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.390
Number two, that the
defendant used the trademark

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.070
in commerce without the company's consent.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.250
And three, the defendant's
use created a likelihood

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.490
of consumer confusion.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.190
The key element is the third one,

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.830
that there is a likelihood that
a consumer will be confused

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.770
about the source of the goods.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.710
And Nike objects, that it has no control

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.627
over the nature and
quality of the Satan Shoes,

00:03:46.627 --> 00:03:48.950
and that it has a reputation and goodwill

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.450
that will be damaged
if MSCHF keeps selling

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.800
these modified Nikes.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.470
And consumers are likely to be confused

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:56.650
by the shoes, and any
defects, objections, or faults

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.260
with the shoes that might
hurt Nike's reputation.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.780
And Nike, of course,
especially objects to the blood

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.190
in the midsole, which
could pose a risk of harm

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:05.200
to the consumer.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.520
But this isn't your garden variety

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.273
trademark infringement case
where some nefarious competitor

00:04:09.273 --> 00:04:11.140
is creating another product,

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.920
intentionally creating it in a way

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.460
that's confusing to people,

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:17.390
creating a bunch of shoes
that have a check mark on it

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.100
that kind of looks like a Nike Swoosh.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.510
Instead, MSCHF actually bought Nikes.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.533
They were originally Nikes.

00:04:22.533 --> 00:04:25.380
It's just that they modified
them after the fact.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.440
Which brings up the most common
defense in a case like this,

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.360
which is called the first sale doctrine.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.300
When people started hearing
about this Nike suit,

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.780
a lot of people were
worried that that meant

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.300
that if Nike can sue you,
you can't buy a consumer good

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.910
and then resell it,
let's say used on eBay,

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.390
or maybe resell it new on Amazon.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.950
But generally, the first sale doctrine

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.580
means that it's legal for an individual

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.440
to resell a trademarked item

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.830
after it has been sold

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.700
by the trademark owner
in an authorized sale.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.900
So when you buy an
authentic pair of Nikes,

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.350
you can usually do what
you want with them.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.310
In fact, anytime you buy a
branded good, it becomes yours.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.560
If you want to buy a book

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.470
and later sell it on eBay,
the author can't stop you.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.380
You can keep it forever

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.640
and maybe give it to
Goodwill, sell it on eBay,

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.580
or throw it in a lake.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.940
It's yours to do with what you want.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.820
And trademark law is
supposed to protect consumers

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.750
from being deceived about
the origin of a product.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.050
Are consumers confused when
they buy the genuine article

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.740
with an authentic trademark?

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.080
Generally, no, they're not.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.420
And that's why a
mark-holder can't stop you

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.190
from reselling a used item.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.290
That's the whole purpose
of the first sale doctrine.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:28.290
And there are a couple of exceptions

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.310
to the first sale doctrine.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.900
For the purposes of Nike's lawsuit,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.970
the most important one
applies when the products sold

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.710
are materially different

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.720
from the company's authorized product.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.540
Nike says that its shoes were materially

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.680
altered to prominently
feature a satanic theme.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.060
And so how do you prove
material difference?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.650
Well, in 2020, one court
described it this way.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:47.980
An alteration is material

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.380
if it changes something about
the product that is relevant

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:53.260
to a consumer's decision
to purchase that product.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.160
That quote is from a case where Maui Jim,

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.860
the sunglass manufacturer,

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.970
sued someone who was
reselling their sunglasses,

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:02.380
but they removed the
lenses from the frames

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.250
and replace them with different lenses.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.080
Generally, either plano
lenses or prescription lenses.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.950
The problem from Maui Jim's perspective

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.920
was that they had patented the lenses

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.860
to promise to wipe out glare and UV rays.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.930
And the Skin Cancer Foundation
officially recommended

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.220
the Maui Jims as an effective UV filter

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.570
for the eyes and surrounding skin.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.700
So Maui Jim didn't want people buying

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.760
these modified sunglasses
without the protections

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.930
that they had designed into
their original glasses.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.450
And Maui Jim successfully
argued that by replacing

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.755
the lenses with something else,

00:06:32.755 --> 00:06:35.390
this reseller had removed
something that factored

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:38.080
into a person's decision
to buy Maui Jim frames.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.180
So to bring it back around
to these Satan Shoes,

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:42.550
Nike is arguing that
confusion has already resulted

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.900
because this unauthorized reseller

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:48.180
and modifier of shoes is
offering original Nike shoes

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:51.150
without the associated benefits
that Nike customers expect.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.840
And it has been materially modified.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.880
Nike says that adding an extra substance

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.010
like blood to the midsole

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.440
of the shoe could pose
safety risks to the consumer.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.810
And of course, Nike also implies

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.110
that lots and lots of
consumers are disgusted

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.560
by the ideas of shoes with blood in them.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.170
And yeah, if you're selling Nike Air Shoes

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.690
they're supposed to have an air pocket

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:11.710
in the sole of the shoe,

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.120
and it's actually filled with liquid,

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.280
regardless of whatever that liquid is,

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.780
that kind of seems like
a material difference.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:20.460
But Nike's second claim is for
false designation of origin,

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.260
which is generally a fancy
name for consumer confusion.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:24.093
According to Nike,

00:07:24.093 --> 00:07:25.950
consumers are already
being misled into believing

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.980
that Nike was deliberately
promoting Satan Shoes.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.820
The company can cite hundreds of posts

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.500
from Christians who are now questioning

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.970
whether Nike is promoting Satan.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.250
They can also find plenty
of people who object

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.030
to having shoes made with blood in them.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:40.080
And I have to admit, when
I first saw the headlines

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.050
for this case, I thought Nike
had manufactured the shoes.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:46.950
There's a prominent white
Nike Swoosh on a black shoe.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:49.460
I thought that Nike had
done this collaboration.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.467
And as Nike says,

00:07:50.467 --> 00:07:53.140
"As an innovative brand that
strives to push the envelope

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.280
and do the right thing,
Nike knows it may not

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.690
please everyone at all time,

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:57.910
but decisions about what products

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.380
to put the Swoosh on belong to Nike."

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.560
But on the other hand, generally,

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.500
when you're talking
about consumer confusion,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.640
you're talking about
point of sale confusion,

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:08.260
that the people who
bought the actual products

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:09.900
were misled into thinking

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.660
that there was some association there.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:15.060
And it's actually sort of
unlikely that the over 600 people

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:18.140
that bought the modified
shoe thought that Nike

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.470
had created the shoe.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.800
It seems like they knew

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.450
that MSCHF was the one
that modified those shoes.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:26.310
So it's hard to argue
that they, the consumers,

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.580
the direct consumers of
these shoes were confused

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:29.640
in any other way.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.320
Though, on the other other hand,

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.180
Nike would argue

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:35.240
that regardless of whether
these consumers were confused,

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.770
downstream consumers, the public at large

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:38.980
will think that Nike had something

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.210
to do with those Satan Shoes

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:43.800
and thus potentially not buy
Nike shoes in the future.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:44.960
And then we get to Nike's third

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.270
and my favorite trademark related claim,

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:49.210
one for trademark dilution.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.750
And I know I joke on this channel

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.640
a lot about claims
being particularly sexy,

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.510
but this claim is actually literally sexy.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.390
And we'll get to that in just a second.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.570
But in 1996, Congress enacted

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.320
the Federal Trademark Dilution Act,

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.940
which made it possible for mark-holders

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.570
to obtain injunctions against
the use of their marks,

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:09.990
even if there is no traditional
trademark infringement.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.750
And the FTDA gives certain mark-holders,

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:14.160
the right to sue when a
third-party uses a mark

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:16.920
in commerce in such a way that
it hurts consumer perception

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.230
of a famous mark.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:20.100
And they're generally
two kinds of dilution,

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:21.850
there's blurring and there's tarnishment.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.070
And blurring is when a
famous mark's distinctiveness

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.350
is harmed because it becomes
or is likely to become

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.850
associated with a similar
mark in a different context.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:31.810
So for example, if Rolex
was suddenly stamped

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:35.290
on golf balls and hotdogs,
in addition to watches,

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.290
then there would be blurring of that mark.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.250
You might associate Rolex with hotdogs

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.840
instead of fancy watches.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.050
And tarnishment, on the other hand,

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:44.540
happens when the famous
mark's reputation is harmed

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:45.918
through an association.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:47.760
Tarnishment creates a harm

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.770
to a famous mark by
associating it with something

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.070
that would damage that reputation.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.650
So normally, that's when
a famous mark is linked

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.350
with something that is
considered offensive

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.770
like pornography or drug use.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:00.547
And courts are especially
hard on expressions that link

00:10:00.547 --> 00:10:02.634
a product to sex.

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:03.467
(sexy music)
I told you,

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:05.020
we were going to get actually sexy

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.240
with this legal claim.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.920
So for example, Barbie won a case

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.540
against a porn company
that wanted to have Barbie

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.000
in their URL.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.090
And the Dallas Cowboy
Cheerleaders won a case

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.550
against the movie, "Debbie Does Dallas"

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.890
because it used Dallas Cowboy
Cheerleader style outfits

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:20.900
in a very adult film.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.160
And a website was not allowed
to use the domain name

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:26.650
candyland.com to identify a
porn site because it tarnished

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.810
and diluted the Hasbro
Candyland trademark associated

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.210
with its board games.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.870
But if the subject is not sex,

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:36.052
then courts are not completely
consistent in how they decide

00:10:36.052 --> 00:10:38.870
whether there is actual
tarnishment and dilution.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.890
So for example, in one case,

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:43.000
parodies involving dog chew
toys were protected speech.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.560
The Ninth Circuit held that a
squeaking dog toy resembling

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.520
a bottle of Jack Daniel's
Whiskey is an expressive work

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.210
entitled to First Amendment protection.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.430
While a Virginia court held

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.700
that Louis Vuitton's
mark was not tarnished

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:57.340
by a company selling Chewy
Vuitton squeaky dog toys.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.500
But on the other hand, Dr. Seuss

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.770
was able to stop publication

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:01.330
of an OJ Simpson trial parody book

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:04.490
called "The Cat Not in
the Hat", by Dr. Juice.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:05.640
The court found the likelihood

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.600
of confusion and stopped publication.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.490
That case involved both
copyright and trademark aspects.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:11.700
You really could write a whole book

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.310
on how Dr. Seuss Enterprises

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:16.350
vigorously defends its
rights through lawsuits.

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:19.010
But in contrast, the
band, Aqua was victorious

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.290
in a battle with Mattel over
the song, "Barbie Girl",

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.570
where the Ninth Circuit held that the song

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.120
about Barbie did not turn
Barbie into a sex object,

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.540
nor did its lyrics tarnish
Barbie's reputation.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.470
But Nike claims had MSCHF's wrongful use

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:32.380
of the Nike asserted marks in connection

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.480
with these satanic imagery

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.960
is likely to cause
dilution by tarnishment.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.020
Which understandably, could theoretically

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:39.630
damage Nike's reputation.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.270
And as I said, courts take
a very puritanical view

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.400
when it comes to associations with sex,

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.740
but we don't know exactly what
the court's going to think

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.300
about using satanic imagery on a shoe,

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.020
whether that's offensive or unsavory

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.170
in the same way that pornography
or criminality would be.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:57.530
But Nike probably has a decent
chance of prevailing on this.

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:59.540
So let's talk about MSCHF's defenses here.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:00.870
In its response to Nike's motion

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:01.990
for a temporary restraining order,

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.670
which I'll get to in a few moments,

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:05.930
MSCHF says that Nike cannot show confusion

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.850
among sophisticated
purchasers of sneakers,

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:10.330
who all knew all along
that this was a collab

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.960
between Lil Nas X and MSCHF,
with no Nike involvement.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.240
But Nike's counter to
this is that Nike's logo

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:18.630
is all over the shoes in question.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.900
And as for Nike's claim that
its brand is being tarnished

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:22.510
by an association with Satan,

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:25.740
MSCHF argues about the
prior shoes that it created.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.040
It created a line of Jesus Shoes,

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:30.470
white shoes with cross iconography

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:33.230
and filled with supposedly
blue holy water,

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:36.130
and says that those shoes
were not universally embraced,

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.210
but Nike didn't try it
and enforce their rights

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:40.557
against that particular modified shoe.

00:12:40.557 --> 00:12:42.810
And on the contrary,
many people were outraged

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:46.740
by the these Jesus Shoes and
labeled them as sacrilegious.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:50.070
And like Nike, MSCHF has
tweets backing up its position.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:51.430
And here's one pointing out that Nike

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:53.020
is named for the Greek Goddess of Victory,

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.630
which at least one Twitter
user found to be offensive.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.030
And here's one saying that the Jesus shoes

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:57.863
made the user sick,

00:12:57.863 --> 00:13:00.800
and he intended throw
away all of his Nike gear.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.470
So Nike can't win with associations

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.050
with other non-satanic deities.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.260
And MSCHF's point here is that
they can probably find tweets

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.220
hammering Nike no matter
what choice they make.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.900
And people have criticized Nike

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:13.460
for manufacturing sneakers in China.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.990
But when Nike criticized
China's forced labor

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.110
camps earlier this year,

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:19.610
Chinese celebrities publicly
cut ties with the company.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:23.000
So Nike is frequently the subject
of debate and controversy.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.860
Those who are convinced
Nike is a horrible company

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.150
are unlikely to be swayed
by the Satan Shoes.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:30.450
And that, of course, brings
us to the First Amendment

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.730
because just because
something is a trademark

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:35.670
or is involved in commerce doesn't mean

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:37.980
that you give up all
First Amendment rights.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.610
Trademarks, of course,
are meant to protect

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:41.210
against consumer confusion.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.960
But in recent years, courts
are increasingly likely to find

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.320
that the First Amendment protects speech,

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:48.400
even when it might naturally
result in some confusion.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.190
And that's a good thing for artists

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:52.230
like Lil Nas X and MSCHF.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.970
Nike of course, claims
that the Satan Shoes

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:55.480
are not a piece of of art,

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.170
and we're not created by artists,

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:59.710
and are just purely a commercial venture.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:01.850
Saying, while MSCHF has
a First Amendment right

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:04.010
to criticize discriminatory social norms,

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:06.000
those norms have nothing
to do with the Nike Swoosh

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.190
and the Nike word mark.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:09.060
But at base, there's clearly some tension

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:11.560
between trying to protect trademarks

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.450
and one's First Amendment
right to expression,

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.030
which takes us to the parody defense.

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:19.520
Just as fair use is a defense
to copyright infringement,

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:20.990
parody is a defense

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:23.650
to some kinds of
trademark dilution claims.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:26.600
But parody in the trademark
context is not easy to prove.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.260
The elements that you
have to show are one,

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.220
an original host work.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.830
Two, the original work must be famous

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.860
or well-known within the
particular target audience.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.830
And three, of the creator
of the derivative work,

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:37.640
the parody must take only
so much of the original work

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.490
as is necessary to bring to
mind the original host work.

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:42.240
And four, the derivative work,

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.030
which conjures up the famous mark

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:46.190
must result a new, original work.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.930
So let's break this down further.

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.270
This is difficult in this context

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:51.000
because the parody has to be making fun

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.410
of a real product here, Nike shoes.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.570
It can't just be a parody

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:57.170
of something else like
religion, for example.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.603
And it has to be obvious to consumers

00:14:58.603 --> 00:15:01.890
that the parody is making a
comment on the real product.

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:03.960
And the second message
must be something like,

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.706
yes, these are authentic Nike shoes,

00:15:05.706 --> 00:15:07.620
and isn't Nike ridiculous

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.630
with the way that they use their brand?

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.900
So there has to be an
element of satire, joking,

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.040
or a irreverent commentary

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.250
that the consumer would understand.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.730
And this is a really interesting issue

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:18.960
for MSCHF because as
we talked about before,

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:20.508
a traditional trademark case cares

00:15:20.508 --> 00:15:22.510
about confusion at the point of sale.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:24.800
Were the people who bought
the Satan Shoes confused

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.830
at all about the source?

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.663
Probably not.

00:15:27.663 --> 00:15:29.750
The buyers knew that
MSCHF had created a parody

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.380
making fun of Nike itself.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.930
The argument being that they're making fun

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:36.840
of all the collaborations
that Nike is willing to do

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.640
that they'll basically
collaborate with anyone,

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.190
even Jesus or Satan.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.610
And there are collectors
who are well aware

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:44.680
of what MSCHF does.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.940
In fact, they may even be aware that MSCHF

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.030
once made Jesus Shoes

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:51.200
with holy water in the midsole,
and Nike didn't object.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.780
And the Jesus Shoe is interesting

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.400
because it added a golden Jesus

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:56.450
on a crucifix as a shoelace charm,

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:59.670
and MSCHF also sourced holy
water from the River Jordan,

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:02.530
which was apparently blessed
by a priest in Brooklyn

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.890
and added it to the sole of the shoe.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.460
And in a press release,

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.860
MSCHF founder said that he was commenting

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.747
on the ridiculous collaborations
that Nike has done.

00:16:10.747 --> 00:16:12.880
"We asked ourselves,
what would a shoe collab

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.300
with Jesus actually look like?

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.840
Obviously, it would let you walk on water.

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:18.187
Well, how can we do that?

00:16:18.187 --> 00:16:21.210
And you pump holy water
into the pocket of air

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.650
of the Air Max 97s.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.590
And with that, you get the Jesus Shoe,

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.200
the holiest collab ever."

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:27.680
And that makes the Jesus Shoe

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.230
and the Satan Shoes
feel more like a parody.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.750
Maybe the Satan Shoe buyers were aware

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:36.110
of this history of weird
collabs and even saw Satan Shoes

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:38.980
as an extension of the
earlier Jesus Shoes.

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.850
Counsel for MSCHF
expanded on this argument

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.310
in the company's TRO
letter, where MSCHF argues

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.020
that the shoes aren't mocking religion,

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.960
they are mocking Nike's reputation.

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.560
And Nike is at once a
global icon and a company

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.270
with a reputation for
shady business practices,

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:56.360
like making shoes using
Chinese sweat shops,

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:59.050
and collaborating with just
about anyone to make a buck.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.460
But this logic may not hold up in court.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:03.730
Nike can respond by saying that sure,

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:07.210
the 666 consumers who purchased
the shoes weren't confused,

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:09.410
but everyone else on
the internet surely was.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.260
And these people matter

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:13.780
because they are future Nike
consumers who are now confused.

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:16.160
They are literally saying,
"Oh no, Nike loves Satan.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.620
I have to burn my Nike's again."

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.110
And that takes us to the motion

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:21.970
for a temporary restraining order.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.470
Nike was lightening
fast with this lawsuit,

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:27.410
filing almost the next day
after the shoes were released.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:28.570
And the day after that,

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:31.130
Nike moved for a temporary
restraining order,

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.380
or an injunction to prevent MSCHF

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:36.820
from doing anything related
to the shoes basically.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.150
Nike wanted a temporary
and permanent injunctive

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:42.320
to prevent MSCHF from
manufacturing, transporting,

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.930
promoting, advertising,
publicizing, distributing,

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.890
ordering for sale, or
selling any products,

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:48.540
including but not limited
to these Satan Shoes

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:49.780
under Nike marks

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:53.370
and/or any marks substantially
indistinguishable therefrom.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.210
Now, we've talked about
TROs a lot on this channel.

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:59.420
Generally, the court only will
issue this emergency relief

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:01.970
when there is irreparable harm that cannot

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.150
be undone by the court.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:07.090
Generally, the idea is if you
can be compensated with money,

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:08.770
even long after the fact,

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.840
that's not irreparable harm.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:15.340
But IP is an area where courts
often find irreparable harm.

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:20.190
It's harm to one reputation or
brand that cannot be undone.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.900
And that's what Nike is saying here,

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:23.548
that their brand is being tarnished-

00:18:23.548 --> 00:18:25.120
(woman screaming)
by an association with Satan.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:28.260
And you can't really
undo that after the fact.

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:30.610
But MSCHF argues that
this is inappropriate

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:35.040
because MSCHF has already
shipped 665 of its 666 pairs

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.770
of shoes, with only one
pair of being held back

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:38.820
for a later raffle.

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:41.120
But it contends that since the
shoes have already shipped,

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:45.010
they've gone out, emergency
relief shouldn't be granted.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:47.280
Well, Nike responded
that even if the company

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:49.213
did all but one of the pairs of shoes,

00:18:49.213 --> 00:18:52.300
the TRO would still be
necessary to prevent

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.120
that one other pair of shoes going out

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:58.450
and to prevent MSCHF from
benefiting from this harmful

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:01.980
and tarnishing action that
they've taken against Nike.

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:04.340
And Nike accuses MSCHF,
probably correctly,

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.870
of quickly shipping the
orders to circumvent

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.130
the possible incoming TRO.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.970
And to add injury to insult,

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:13.110
MSCHF is now selling a T-shirt bearing

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:16.250
the front page of Nike's
complaint on the shirt.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.410
That is some creative marketing there.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:20.790
And of course, Nike accused MSCHF

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:22.760
of deliberately trying
to stir up controversy

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.500
by promoting the T-shirt and going forward

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.690
with the shoe sale,

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.650
despite having noticed that Nike believed

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:29.980
that this was trademark infringement.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:30.882
But at the same time,

00:19:30.882 --> 00:19:34.170
Nike didn't technically notify MSCHF

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:36.720
by letter or phone call, that
had objected to the shoes.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:39.370
The company just simply
went forward with a lawsuit

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.380
on the same day of the sale.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.380
But just like Nike,

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.140
the court moved lightening fast.

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:45.130
And within a day,

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:46.620
issued a temporary restraining order,

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.450
preventing MSCHF from really
doing anything related

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.500
to the shoes.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.760
But here, it's hard to unring the bell.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:53.650
The shoes are out.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:57.010
MSCHF has really benefited
from all of the publicity

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.390
that it has gotten related
to the Satan Shoes.

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:01.650
And the associations have been made.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.970
Now, the court hasn't made a determination

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.770
on the merits, a final one.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:08.210
It found that Nike was likely to prevail

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.690
if this indeed goes forward,

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:14.500
but MSCHF will be able to
present all of its arguments,

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.071
even those related to the
First Amendment issues

00:20:17.071 --> 00:20:20.140
in briefing related to
a preliminary injunction

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.440
and eventually, the trial itself.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:24.700
But if you want to shoot
a Satan-themed music video

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.090
that may or may not be a parody,

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:28.050
you'll need to learn how
to shoot great video.

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:29.460
And no one does that
better than my friend,

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.130
Marques Brownlee who a new class

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:34.400
on Skillshare called "Script,
Shoot, &amp; Edit with MKBHD".

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.020
From initial concept to final cut,

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:38.220
Marques will share his creative process,

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.150
